  "$comment": "Amazon Berkeley Objects' product types, as the kind a detector should name for the listing's main picture (docs/specs/camera-search.md, Measures). Each type maps to one of the shop's category codes (sold) or to one of the common objects the shop does not sell (notSold) — the list the detector is also given, so the shop can say so. ABO's types are noisy (ground coffee under COFFEE_MAKER, socks under LUGGAGE), so a listing is taken only when its English name matches 'name' and not 'not', case-insensitive; a type may list several rules, tried in order. A type in neither list is not used: its picture would have no right answer. No laptop is taken from ABO: its few listings with a large picture are stands and cables, and the author's desk photographs carry one.",
